//Aim
To perform data aggregation and apply statistical functions in Tableau for better data analysis.

//Algorithm
1. Open Tableau Public.
2. Connect to the dataset.
3. Drag required fields into rows and columns.
4. Apply aggregation functions.
5. Use statistical measures.
6. Analyze and save the results.

Program
1 import pandas as pd
2
3 # Load dataset
4 data = pd.read_csv("sales_data.csv")
5
6 # Total Sales
7 print("Total Sales:", data["Sales"].sum())
8
9 # Average Sales
10 print("Average Sales:", data["Sales"].mean())
11
12 # Minimum Sales
13 print("Minimum Sales:", data["Sales"].min())
14
15 # Maximum Sales
16 print("Maximum Sales:", data["Sales"].max())
18 # Group by Category
19 print("\nSales by Category:")
20 print(data.groupby("Category")["Sales"].sum())

//Sample Output
The output displays total sales, average sales, minimum sales, maximum sales and sales grouped
by category.

Result
Thus, data aggregation and statistical analysis were successfully performed using Tableau.
